messages.content:
{
  "message": "Thanks — I’ve verified your identity and logged it. I can run the card/account diagnostics now, but I need one more thing to find the right cards quickly. Please provide the last 4 digits of each debit card that was declined and (if you remember) the approximate time and merchant name for each decline. Also confirm whether all three cards are Rho‑Bank cards (do they show the Rho logo?).\n\nIf you’d rather not share last 4s, tell me whether you have more than one Rho checking account and which checking account you want me to check. Once I have that, I’ll look up the card statuses, fraud/velocity flags, and recent pending transactions and tell you what I find and next steps (including lifting a temporary velocity block if present)."
}

{
  "message": "Thanks — I’ve verified you and logged it. I can’t run the bank’s card/account diagnostics without either the debit card’s last 4 digits or the checking account ID for your Blue Account. I understand you don’t want to share the last 4 here, so you have two secure options — please pick one and I’ll proceed:",
  "options": [
    {
      "option_id": "provide_account_id",
      "description": "Provide the Blue Account checking account ID (found in the app) and I will run diagnostics now. How to find it in the app: Accounts → select your Blue Account → Account details (or Settings) → look for “Account ID” or “Account number.” Paste that ID here."
    },
    {
      "option_id": "read_last4_privately",
      "description": "Read the last 4 digits from the physical card and share them here. I will use that to locate the exact card and run diagnostics (card status, fraud/velocity flags, account status, pending authorizations) and — if there’s a temporary velocity block and you want it lifted — I can lift it now."
    },
    {
      "option_id": "self_check_and_workarounds",
      "description": "You don’t provide identifiers. I’ll continue guiding you to self‑check and try immediate workarounds (chip/contactless, signature vs PIN, mobile wallet, confirm available balance and pending holds in the app). Choose this if you want step‑by‑step help doing that right now."
    },
    {
      "option_id": "transfer_to_human",
      "description": "If you prefer not to share any identifiers here and want a human to help (including in‑line secure channels), I can transfer you to a human agent. Would you like me to do that?"
    }
  ],
  "note": "Once you provide either the account ID or the last 4, I’ll run the diagnostics and report back what’s causing the CODE 05 for the $85 restaurant charge and what immediate actions we can take (including lifting a temporary velocity block if eligible)."
}

{
  "message": "I can unfreeze your Blue card for you. I already have your identity verification on file, but to perform the unfreeze I need to locate the exact card in our system. Please choose one of the two options below so I can proceed:",
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "provide_last4",
      "text": "Provide the last 4 digits of the Blue Account debit card (printed on the physical card). I will use that to locate the card and unfreeze it immediately."
    },
    {
      "id": "provide_account_id",
      "text": "Provide the Blue Account checking account ID (from the app). I will look up all debit cards for that account and unfreeze the correct one."
    },
    {
      "id": "self_unfreeze_in_app",
      "text": "I’ll walk you through unfreezing the card in the Rho app yourself (you already indicated you have the card)."
    }
  ],
  "app_unfreeze_steps": [
    "Open the Rho app → Accounts → select your Blue Account.",
    "Tap Cards or Card Settings and find the Blue physical card (match by the last 4 on your card).",
    "If you see a Freeze/Unfreeze toggle, switch it to Unfreeze (or tap Unfreeze).",
    "Confirm the action when prompted. The card should be usable immediately after unfreezing.",
    "If you see any error or a message about a security hold, copy the exact wording and tell me — I’ll advise next steps."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "If you want me to proceed here, please provide either the last 4 digits or the account ID. I will then unfreeze the card immediately and confirm when it’s active.",
    "If you froze the card and later reported it lost or stolen (closed) instead of a temporary freeze, I cannot unfreeze a closed card — let me know if you reported it lost/stolen at any point.",
    "If there’s also a temporary velocity or bank‑initiated fraud block, unfreezing may not by itself allow transactions; if that’s the case I’ll tell you what additional steps are needed.",
    "Would you like me to unfreeze only the Blue card or both Blue and Green once you provide identifiers?"
  ]
}

{
  "message": "Great — glad the Blue card is active. Here’s exactly what to do next and what to tell me if the payment still declines, plus quick guidance for your other cards.",
  "if_payment_still_declines": {
    "what_to_tell_me_immediately": [
      "Exact decline message shown on the terminal (copy the wording) and the code (you earlier saw CODE 05 — confirm if it shows again).",
      "Merchant name and which register/terminal you used (e.g., “Main register, Server #3”).",
      "Exact time of the decline (HH:MM) and the amount attempted.",
      "Which authorization method you tried (chip, contactless/tap, swipe, or mobile wallet) and whether you tried signature vs PIN.",
      "Whether the app now shows the card as ACTIVE and any in‑app messages or alerts you see."
    ],
    "helpful_optional_items": [
      "A quick photo/screenshot of the terminal decline screen (if you can capture it safely).",
      "If you want me to run diagnostics, provide either the last 4 digits of the Blue card or the Blue Account checking account ID so I can look up card status, fraud/velocity flags, and pending authorizations."
    ],
    "what_i_can_do_if_you_provide_info": "If you provide the last 4 or account ID I can look up card and account flags and, if it’s a temporary velocity block or a customer‑initiated fraud alert, clear it for you immediately. If there’s a bank‑initiated security hold I cannot clear it and I’ll escalate you to our security team."
  },
  "quick_troubleshooting_if_declines_again_right_now": [
    "Try chip or contactless tap (if you swiped, try chip/contactless) or try a different register.",
    "If possible, try signature authorization instead of PIN.",
    "Try your mobile wallet (Apple/Google Pay) if the card is stored there.",
    "Wait 5–15 minutes and retry (temporary velocity/network blocks often clear quickly).",
    "Check the app for available balance and pending authorizations — if available < charge, move funds or use another payment method."
  ],
  "about_your_other_cards": {
    "what_to_check": [
      "Open the app → Accounts → select the other account(s) (Green Account and the third card’s account) → Cards/Card Settings and check each card’s status (ACTIVE, FROZEN, PENDING, or CLOSED).",
      "Match the last‑4 on each card to the app to be sure you’re checking the right one."
    ],
    "how_to_unfreeze_your_other_cards": [
      "You can unfreeze the Green card (and any other frozen card) the same way you did the Blue: locate the Freeze/Unfreeze toggle on the card detail page and switch to Unfreeze.",
      "If you’d prefer, I can unfreeze any frozen card for you from here — I already have your identity verified. To do that I’ll need the last 4 of the card you want unfrozen or the checking account ID."
    ],
    "safety_and_follow_up": [
      "If any card shows CLOSED or shows language like “reported lost/stolen,” do NOT unfreeze — closed/lost/stolen cards cannot be reactivated and need replacement.",
      "If any card screen shows a bank‑initiated security hold or language about contacting support/security, tell me the exact wording — I cannot clear bank‑initiated holds and will transfer you to our security team for further review.",
      "After you unfreeze a card and confirm it works, consider re‑freezing it later if you prefer that protection when you’re not using it."
    ]
  },
  "offer_and_next_steps": {
    "options": [
      "Try the restaurant payment now and come back with the info above if it still declines.",
      "If you want me to unfreeze the Green (or any other frozen) card for you now, say which card and provide last 4 or the account ID and I’ll unfreeze it immediately.",
      "If the decline persists and you want me to diagnose it here, provide the last 4 of the Blue card or the Blue Account ID and I’ll run the diagnostics and clear any eligible velocity block."
    ],
    "final_note": "I’m here while you retry — if it fails, tell me the terminal wording/time/merchant and whether you tried chip/contactless/signature. If all is good after the retry, tell me and I’ll help you unfreeze the Green card if you want."
  }
}
